    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0550" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg466"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1903-01-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1021.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 1020 of the 3d
                    instant, I have the honor to inform you that having ascertained yesterday that
                    Lord <pb facs="0551" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/> Lansdowne would like to see me
                    late in the afternoon I called upon him at the foreign office at half-past 6,
                    when he handed me a note, which I have already cabled you in full, containing
                    the reply of His Majesty’s Government to the communication which I addressed to
                    his lordship on the 1st instant. A copy of this note is inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d458-a1.xml" xpointer="d458-a1"/>
            </div>
